 ```
 
+`strip_prefix(s, prefix)` and `strip_suffix(s, suffix)` (0.16) return
+`s` without that prefix or suffix, as a view of `s`, in an `Option`:
+`None` when `s` does not start (end) with it; an empty prefix gives
+`Some(s)`, the whole of `s` gives `Some("")`.
+
+```tach
+use std::{strip_prefix, strip_suffix};
+
+fn main() -> i32 {
+    for line in ["--name=ada", "--verbose", "file.tach", "-x"] {
+        if let Some(opt) = strip_prefix(line, "--") {
+            println(f"option {opt}");
+        } else if let Some(stem) = strip_suffix(line, ".tach") {
+            println(f"source {stem}");
+        } else {
+            println(f"other {line}");
+        }
+    }
+    0
+}
+```
+```out
+option name=ada
+option verbose
+source file
+other -x
+```
